# Modal title & subtext

Every modal / dialog in the app (confirm dialogs, `Add prompt`, `Add
competitor`, `Track prompt`, `Connect fixes`, subscription, setup wizard,
`Website audit settings`, `New project`, etc.) must use one consistent header
typography. Consistency across modals matters more than per-modal creativity.

## Fixed typography — never change

- **Title** — `text-[16px] font-semibold text-gray-900` (16px, semibold, never
  18px / bold, never 15px).
- **Subtext** (the descriptive line under the title) —
  `text-[14px] font-normal text-gray-500` (14px, regular weight, never
  13px, never `font-medium` / `font-semibold`).

These are exported from the shared modal component so they can be reused
verbatim:

```
src/components/HLModal.jsx  →  export const modalTitle, modalSubtext
```

```jsx
import { modalTitle, modalSubtext } from '../HLModal.jsx' // adjust relative depth

<h2 className={modalTitle}>Add prompt</h2>
<p className={modalSubtext}>Use your own prompt or start from an AI-suggested prompt.</p>
```

Inline usage must match exactly:

```jsx
<h2 className="text-[16px] font-semibold text-gray-900">Add competitor</h2>
<p className="text-[14px] font-normal text-gray-500">Add a brand to track alongside yours.</p>
```

## Rules

- The modal **title** is the single top heading of the dialog — style it
  `text-[16px] font-semibold text-gray-900`. Do not use `text-[18px]`,
  `font-bold`, or `text-[15px]` for a modal title.
- The **subtext** directly under the title is `text-[14px] font-normal
  text-gray-500`. Do not make it 13px or give it `font-medium`.
- Sentence case for both (see the sentence-casing rule).
- This applies whether the modal is built on `HLModal` or as a bespoke
  `createPortal` / `role="dialog"` dialog.

## Primary CTA — text only, no icon

The primary action button in a modal footer is **text only** — never add a
leading or trailing icon (no `Check`, `ChevronRight`, `CreditCard`, `RefreshCw`,
`ArrowRight`, etc.).

```jsx
// Good
<button className="h-9 px-4 rounded-lg bg-primary-600 hover:bg-primary-700 text-white text-[13px] font-semibold">
  Add competitor
</button>

// Bad — icon in the primary CTA
<button className="... inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 ...">
  <Check size={14} /> Add competitor
</button>
```

- Remove `inline-flex items-center gap-1.5` icon wrappers from the primary CTA
  when there is no longer an icon (keep `inline-flex items-center justify-center`
  only if needed for alignment).
- This applies to the primary CTA specifically. Secondary/tertiary buttons
  (e.g. a `← Previous step` back button) may keep an icon if it aids meaning,
  but prefer text-only for consistency.

## Scope

- Applies to the modal's own header only. Section headings, card titles, and
  step labels **inside** the modal body keep their own styling — do not force
  them to 16px/14px.
- The macOS-style file picker (`DesktopAccessModal`) is an OS-chrome mimic, not
  a product modal, and is exempt from this rule.

## Before finishing modal work

- [ ] Title is `text-[16px] font-semibold text-gray-900`.
- [ ] Subtext is `text-[14px] font-normal text-gray-500`.
- [ ] No `text-[18px]` / `font-bold` / `text-[15px]` / 13px title-or-subtext left
      on the modal header.
- [ ] Reused `modalTitle` / `modalSubtext` (or the exact classes) instead of a
      bespoke size.
- [ ] Primary CTA is text only — no leading/trailing icon.
